[OP wants to know what to do now, since he is not experienced enough
for quest.]

It is pretty normal, at least for me, to find the transporter when my
character is still only XL 12 or 13.  When this happens, there are a
few good ways to pick up the experience I need to do the quest.  The
first way is to quaff some potions of gain level.  More commonly, I
save those, and go down and clear out Medusa and, if still needed, the
castle.  Have you ever made it to those levels before?  They are very
exciting, especially the first few times.

I think it goes without saying that you need to be careful, now more
than ever.  For Medusa, of course, you need a way to cross water, and
either a blindfold or reflection.  Or, you can skip Medusa for now and
dig down to the castle.  Do you know the tune yet?  If not, you still
need a way of crossing water.

It would be a good idea to fix up your cloak before it gets any more
rotted and disappears on you.  Review the enchantment section of the
armor spoiler to learn about fixing rot (and preventing future rot.)

Have you blessed your unicorn horn?

Do you know the ID spell or have some scrolls of ID you could bless, to
find out what rings you've got?  Levitation, conflict, etc would be
handy about now.

Your AC could stand to go quite a bit lower... don't suppose you've
found any t-shirts or hawaiian shirts to enchant?  How about a
wizard-appropriate hat?

I'm not that familiar with wizards, but I believe it's traditional to
pick a few schools of magic to #enhance in... what spells do you know?
Are you #enhancing in to an appropriate level in their schools of
magic?

If you just need something to do, you could go find the touchstone in
mine's end and work on identifying some of those gems.  Gems are a
great way to get cash for additional priest donations, if there are
enough shopkeepers who will buy them.

OK, probably other people will have smarter stuff to say.  I hope this
gives you some ideas.



